      "id": "stg_theory",
      "type": "lecture",
      "title": "Concepto Teórico: Pasado Continuo",
      "parts": [
        { "visual": "Usamos el Pasado Continuo para describir una acción que ESTABA en progreso en un momento específico del pasado. Estructura: was / were + verbo-ing.", "audio": "We use the Past Continuous to describe an action that WAS in progress at a specific time in the past. Structure: was or were plus verb with ing." },
        { "visual": "Ejemplos: I was working at 8 AM (Yo estaba trabajando a las 8 AM). They were having a meeting yesterday at 3 PM (Ellos estaban teniendo una reunión ayer a las 3 PM). Negativo: wasn't / weren't.", "audio": "Examples: I was working at 8 AM. They were having a meeting yesterday at 3 PM. Negative: wasn't or weren't." }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "stg_quiz_choice",
